WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.353 --> 00:00:19.416
Shortly after the mayor left for Arras, Fantine awoke.

2
00:00:20.276 --> 00:00:22.378
She had passed a long, difficult night.

3
00:00:22.398 --> 00:00:24.519
"How are you this morning?"

4
00:00:24.939 --> 00:00:28.602
asked Sister Simplice, one of two nuns who worked at the infirmary.

5
00:00:28.622 --> 00:00:32.945
"I want to see Mayor Madeleine," Fantine said weakly.

6
00:00:33.746 --> 00:00:35.748
"Later," said Sister Simplice.

7
00:00:36.308 --> 00:00:39.731
"You know he comes to visit you every day promptly at three o'clock."

8
00:00:40.632 --> 00:00:46.937
Fantine rested for the next several hours, but by two thirty she was agitated and kept asking Sister

9
00:00:46.977 --> 00:00:48.098
Simplice the time.

10
00:00:49.099 --> 00:00:50.240
The clock struck three.

11
00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:56.385
Fantine, who was usually too weak to turn over in bed, sat up and looked at the door.

12
00:00:57.266 --> 00:00:59.808
Nobody came in; the door did not open.

13
00:01:00.508 --> 00:01:04.771
Finally after 15 minutes of anticipation, Fantine lay down.

14
00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:08.313
Sister Simplice was surprised that the mayor was late.

15
00:01:10.174 --> 00:01:14.736
At six o'clock she sent a servant to the factory to ask if the mayor would soon be

16
00:01:14.776 --> 00:01:15.957
coming to the infirmary.

17
00:01:16.817 --> 00:01:21.660
The servant returned and reported that Madeleine had left by carriage early that morning.

18
00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:25.182
"I can hear you talking about Mayor Madeleine!"

19
00:01:25.462 --> 00:01:26.483
Fantine called out.

20
00:01:26.503 --> 00:01:28.324
"Why hasn't he come?"

21
00:01:29.492 --> 00:01:32.133
"He has gone away," said Sister Simplice.

22
00:01:33.353 --> 00:01:35.874
Fantine sprang up and sat on the edge of her bed.

23
00:01:35.894 --> 00:01:38.054
"He must have gone to fetch Cosette!

24
00:01:39.295 --> 00:01:41.575
I think they'll be back by tomorrow, don't you?"

25
00:01:42.736 --> 00:01:47.277
Sister Simplice did not contradict Fantine but helped her back under the covers.

26
00:01:47.297 --> 00:01:49.998
"You are very sick, my child.

27
00:01:50.618 --> 00:01:52.218
Try to rest and don't talk."

28
00:01:53.258 --> 00:01:55.919
Fantine fell asleep with a smile on her face.

29
00:01:56.599 --> 00:02:01.569
The doctor arrived at about eight o'clock, and Fantine opened her eyes as he took her pulse.

30
00:02:04.229 --> 00:02:06.770
"Oh, there's no need for that," she said.

31
00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:08.211
"I'm cured!

32
00:02:08.851 --> 00:02:10.891
Cosette is coming tomorrow!"

33
00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:15.392
The doctor was surprised to find that Fantine really did appear to be better.

34
00:02:16.353 --> 00:02:21.754
Her pulse was stronger, and new life seemed to flow through the seriously ill young woman.

35
00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:28.900
As the doctor left, he said to Sister Simplice, "If the mayor does bring Cosette tomorrow, who knows

36
00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:29.601
what will happen?

37
00:02:30.481 --> 00:02:34.984
I've seen happiness cure some people, and perhaps it will do so in this case."

38
00:02:36.084 --> 00:02:39.627
Meanwhile the mayor had finally reached Arras at eight o'clock that night.

39
00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:43.369
The lights were still on in the courthouse, so he went inside.

40
00:02:43.929 --> 00:02:46.771
A police officer stood near the closed door of the courtroom.

41
00:02:46.791 --> 00:02:49.712
"You can't go in, monsieur," said the policeman.

42
00:02:49.732 --> 00:02:51.153
"The courtroom is full."

43
00:02:51.173 --> 00:02:53.735
"What? There are no more seats?"

44
00:02:54.655 --> 00:02:55.816
The policeman hesitated.

45
00:02:56.492 --> 00:03:00.556
"There are some seats behind the judge, but he only allows public officials to sit there."

46
00:03:02.297 --> 00:03:05.140
Madeleine crossed the hall and went slowly down the stairs.

47
00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.481
He seemed to hesitate on every step.

48
00:03:08.402 --> 00:03:13.186
When he reached the landing, he stopped and wrote Mayor Madeleine on a piece of paper.

49
00:03:13.827 --> 00:03:16.609
Then he went back and handed this paper to the policeman.

50
00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:20.893
"Take that to the judge," said the mayor in a commanding voice.

51
00:03:21.794 --> 00:03:26.994
The policeman showed the paper to the judge and whispered, "This gentleman would like to witness the trial."

52
00:03:27.894 --> 00:03:32.898
The judge was familiar with Mayor Madeleine's name and knew that he was universally admired.

53
00:03:32.918 --> 00:03:35.860
"Allow him to enter," said the judge.

54
00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:41.723
A few minutes later Madeleine followed the policeman into the courtroom and took a seat behind the judge.

55
00:03:42.704 --> 00:03:48.508
Terrified that someone might see him, he slouched behind a pile of the judge's papers, where he was

56
00:03:48.548 --> 00:03:50.569
still able to view most of the courtroom.

57
00:03:52.291 --> 00:03:57.927
He noticed that Monsieur Bamatabois, who had thrown the snow at Fantine, was one of the jurors.

58
00:03:59.068 --> 00:04:02.472
Madeleine stared at the accused man, Champmathieu.

59
00:04:03.132 --> 00:04:06.135
He felt as if he were looking at an older version of himself.

60
00:04:07.016 --> 00:04:09.618
There was definitely a resemblance between the two men.

61
00:04:10.239 --> 00:04:13.081
The prosecuting attorney started questioning Champmathieu.

62
00:04:13.101 --> 00:04:18.546
"First, did you climb the wall, break off the tree branch, and steal the apples?

63
00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:24.365
And second, are you the former convict known as Jean Valjean?"

64
00:04:24.385 --> 00:04:26.626
"I never stole anything!"

65
00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:27.886
said Champmathieu.

66
00:04:27.906 --> 00:04:33.227
"I found the broken branch on the ground and picked it up, little knowing what trouble it would

67
00:04:33.267 --> 00:04:33.788
cause me.

68
00:04:34.548 --> 00:04:38.469
You talk about someone named Jean Valjean, but I don't know who that is.

69
00:04:39.409 --> 00:04:40.690
My name is Champmathieu."

70
00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.110
The prosecuting attorney addressed the judge.

71
00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:52.201
"Since the accused man is denying the charges, we request that you call the convicts, Brevet, Cochepaille, and

72
00:04:52.281 --> 00:04:54.282
Chenildieu, to the witness stand.

73
00:04:55.162 --> 00:05:00.745
I would like to ask them—as well as the police officer Javert—to identify this man."

74
00:05:00.765 --> 00:05:07.608
"As you recall," said the judge, "we gave Javert permission to leave after he made his statement.

75
00:05:08.588 --> 00:05:09.949
But I will call the others."

76
00:05:10.789 --> 00:05:15.691
The three convicts were led into the courtroom, and the judge asked each of them to identify the

77
00:05:15.732 --> 00:05:16.472
accused man.

78
00:05:17.108 --> 00:05:20.029
The convicts were all certain that the man was Jean Valjean.

79
00:05:20.049 --> 00:05:25.912
"Prisoner, you have listened to these men identify you as Jean Valjean," said the judge.

80
00:05:26.572 --> 00:05:27.973
"What do you have to say?"

81
00:05:29.013 --> 00:05:31.474
The confused old man simply laughed.

82
00:05:32.194 --> 00:05:35.916
A buzz of noise filled the courtroom as the spectators started talking.

83
00:05:37.277 --> 00:05:40.838
It was obvious that Champmathieu was going to be found guilty.

84
00:05:40.858 --> 00:05:43.979
"Officers, enforce order in the court!"

85
00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:45.000
said the judge.

86
00:05:45.668 --> 00:05:47.070
"I'm about to sum up the case."

87
00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:50.092
At this moment there was a movement near the judge.

88
00:05:50.873 --> 00:05:54.636
Mayor Madeleine slowly stood up and walked to the center of the courtroom.

89
00:05:54.656 --> 00:06:00.261
"Brevet, Chenildieu, and Cochepaille, look at me!"

90
00:06:01.262 --> 00:06:07.808
The judge, Monsieur Bamatabois, and a dozen other people in the courtroom all exclaimed at once, "Mayor Madeleine!"

91
00:06:07.828 --> 00:06:10.050
"Don't you recognize me?"

92
00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.832
he said to the three prisoners.

93
00:06:12.444 --> 00:06:17.007
All three looked confused and indicated with a shake of the head that they did not know him.

94
00:06:17.927 --> 00:06:19.628
Madeleine turned toward the judge.

95
00:06:19.648 --> 00:06:24.250
"Your Honor, release the accused man and order my arrest.

96
00:06:25.111 --> 00:06:29.433
He is not the man whom you seek because I am Jean Valjean."

97
00:06:30.914 --> 00:06:32.895
The courtroom went totally silent.

98
00:06:33.715 --> 00:06:35.616
The judge gave the mayor a look of pity.

99
00:06:35.636 --> 00:06:37.457
"Is there a doctor here?

100
00:06:38.038 --> 00:06:40.079
Mayor Madeleine appears to be ill."

101
00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:44.301
"Thank you, Your Honor," said the mayor, "but I am not ill.

102
00:06:44.941 --> 00:06:49.322
You were on the verge of making a huge mistake, and I will prove it to you."

103
00:06:49.902 --> 00:06:52.303
Then Madeleine turned back to the three convicts.

104
00:06:52.323 --> 00:06:57.584
"Brevet, do you remember those checkered knit suspenders you always wore on the prison ship?"

105
00:06:58.365 --> 00:07:00.585
Brevet started as if struck by lightning.

106
00:07:00.605 --> 00:07:06.067
"Chenildieu," said the mayor, "you have a large scar on your left shoulder, don't you?"

107
00:07:06.087 --> 00:07:07.407
"That's true!"

108
00:07:07.787 --> 00:07:08.827
exclaimed Chenildieu.

109
00:07:08.847 --> 00:07:16.068
"And, Cochepaille, you have a blue tattoo on your left arm with the date March 1, 1815."

110
00:07:17.009 --> 00:07:20.311
Cochepaille rolled up his sleeve and revealed the tattoo.

111
00:07:21.532 --> 00:07:24.194
The unhappy mayor addressed the entire courtroom.

112
00:07:24.214 --> 00:07:30.359
"You can clearly see that I am Jean Valjean, and I admit that I robbed the chimney sweep

113
00:07:30.399 --> 00:07:31.140
Little Gervais."

114
00:07:32.121 --> 00:07:36.104
He gave a smile of triumph, but it was also a smile of despair.

115
00:07:37.008 --> 00:07:40.949
Everyone in the courtroom was stunned, and no one seemed to know what to do.

116
00:07:40.969 --> 00:07:44.890
"I won't disturb this trial anymore," continued Valjean.

117
00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:49.112
"I am leaving because I have not been arrested, and I have many things to do.

118
00:07:49.852 --> 00:07:54.914
The prosecuting attorney knows who I am and where I live, so he'll have me arrested when he

119
00:07:54.974 --> 00:08:02.096
chooses." Valjean left the courtroom, and less than an hour later, all charges were dropped against
